IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Veterans' Entitlements Act 1986 (Commonwealth of Australia) -- what the veteran (and the veteran's widow or widower) meets:
-- whether a new claim can still be made under this Act (s 12AA, from 1 July 2026) and whether an injury is the VEA's or the
-- MRCA's (s 9A); a veteran's pension age (s 5QA); qualifying service (s 7A(1)(a)); eligibility for the age service pension and the
-- invalidity service pension, with the residence rule for Commonwealth and allied veterans (ss 36, 37, 36H); the provisional
-- commencement day (s 36B); which rate of disability pension a veteran is paid -- general, extreme disablement adjustment,
-- intermediate or special (TPI) -- and how much (ss 22, 23, 24); the war widow's or widower's pension paid without a claim and its
-- rate (ss 13A, 30(1)); telling the Department of a change (s 54); and asking for review (ss 57, 57A, 135(5), 175).
--
-- SEAT: the veteran -- and, for ss 13A and 30, the widow or widower of a veteran. "Can I still claim under the VEA? Am I eligible
-- for a service pension? What rate of disability pension am I on? Does my partner get a war widow's pension when I die? How do I
-- ask for a review?" The Repatriation Commission's and the Secretary's decisions are asked as facts.
--
-- Edition: Compilation No. 199, compilation date 1 July 2026, includes amendments up to Act No. 17, 2025 and Act No. 31, 2026
-- (register id C2026C00275, in 4 volumes), as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/C2004A03268.txt.
--
-- INPUTS SET OUTSIDE THE TEXT. The pension rates in ss 22(3), 22(4), 23(4), 24(4) and 30(1) are indexed twice a year (s 198 and
-- Part IIIB Division 18): the figures printed in the compilation ($338.94, $510.40, $619.80, $1,595.66; $35 and $25.60) may not be
-- the figures in force, so the rates in force are inputs. The degree of incapacity and the impairment and lifestyle ratings are the
-- Commission's under the Approved Guide (s 29, not deposited); permanent incapacity for work is the Commission's s 37AA
-- determination (not deposited); the MRCA commencement date is the MRCA's. All are asked as facts.
--
-- NOT ENCODED. The service pension rate (the Rate Calculator in Schedule 6, the income and assets tests) and its supplements; the
-- partner service pension (s 38), income support supplement (Part IIIA), veteran payment, pension bonus (Part IIIAB); the special
-- rate's rehabilitation and offsetting rules (ss 23(5), (6), 24(5)-(6), 25A, 115D); temporary special rate (s 25), s 26
-- reductions, s 27 specific disability amounts, compensation offsets (Division 5A); the dependant child rate (s 30(2)); Part IV
-- (peacekeepers and the Forces), Part V (treatment), the allowances and benefits of Parts VI and VIA; the Veterans' Review Board
-- procedure (it now sits under Chapter 8 of the MRCA); information, offences and machinery.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written from the veteran's seat with the 2026-10-18 defaults. No pipeline, no coverage table, no
-- independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Veterans' Entitlements Act 1986 -- the veteran's questions`

§§ `Date helpers`

-- A day some number of months after another (the same day of the month, or the last day of a shorter month).
GIVEN `y` IS A NUMBER
      `m` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days in the month` MEANS
    IF `m` EQUALS 12
    THEN DATE_SERIAL (Date 1 1 (`y` PLUS 1)) MINUS DATE_SERIAL (Date 1 12 `y`)
    ELSE DATE_SERIAL (Date 1 (`m` PLUS 1) `y`) MINUS DATE_SERIAL (Date 1 `m` `y`)

GIVEN `d` IS A DATE
      `n` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the day months after` MEANS
    Date (min (DATE_DAY `d`) (`the days in the month` `year` `month`)) `month` `year`
    WHERE
        `count` MEANS (DATE_MONTH `d` MINUS 1) PLUS `n`
        `year` MEANS DATE_YEAR `d` PLUS FLOOR (`count` DIVIDED BY 12)
        `month` MEANS (`count` MINUS (12 TIMES FLOOR (`count` DIVIDED BY 12))) PLUS 1

-- Complete months of age on a day (a birthday month is complete on the day of the month the person was born).
GIVEN `born` IS A DATE
      `on` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`complete months of age` MEANS
    IF DATE_DAY `on` AT LEAST DATE_DAY `born`
    THEN `whole`
    ELSE `whole` MINUS 1
    WHERE
        `whole` MEANS ((DATE_YEAR `on` MINUS DATE_YEAR `born`) TIMES 12) PLUS (DATE_MONTH `on` MINUS DATE_MONTH `born`)

§§ `ss 12AA, 9A -- can I still claim under this Act`

-- s 12AA: "Despite anything else in this Act: (a) a claim or application may not be made under any of the following on or after
-- the date of commencement: (i) Part II (other than Division 2A); (ii) Part IV; (iii) section 111 (other than in respect of
-- bereavement payment under section 98AA); (iv) a legislative instrument made under section 105 or 106". s 5Q: "date of
-- commencement means 1 July 2026." Note 1: such claims "will be able to be made under the MRCA". Part II is the disability pension
-- and the war widow's and widower's pension; Part III (service pensions) and Part IIIA (income support supplement) are not
-- listed, so claims under them continue.
DECLARE `What I want to claim` IS ONE OF
    `a disability pension, or an increase in it, for a war-caused injury or disease (Part II)`
    `a war widow's or widower's pension, or an orphan's pension (Part II)`
    `a verification determination as a reinstated pensioner (Part II Division 2A)`
    `a pension under Part IV (members of the Forces and peacekeepers)`
    `an allowance or benefit under s 111 (other than bereavement payment)`
    `an age or invalidity service pension (Part III)`
    `a partner service pension (Part III) or income support supplement (Part IIIA)`

DECLARE `Can I claim under the VEA` IS ONE OF
    `yes: this claim can still be made under the Veterans' Entitlements Act`
    `no: from 1 July 2026 this claim cannot be made under the VEA (s 12AA); it is made under the MRCA instead`

@export Can I still make this claim under the Veterans' Entitlements Act, or must it go under the MRCA (s 12AA)?
GIVEN `what` IS A `What I want to claim` @desc What you want to claim
      `the day I claim` IS A DATE @desc The day you would make the claim or application
GIVETH A `Can I claim under the VEA`
`Can I claim this under the VEA` MEANS
    IF `the day I claim` AT LEAST Date 1 7 2026 AND `it is closed by s 12AA`
    THEN `no: from 1 July 2026 this claim cannot be made under the VEA (s 12AA); it is made under the MRCA instead`
    ELSE `yes: this claim can still be made under the Veterans' Entitlements Act`
    WHERE
        `it is closed by s 12AA` MEANS
            CONSIDER `what`
            WHEN `a disability pension, or an increase in it, for a war-caused injury or disease (Part II)` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `a war widow's or widower's pension, or an orphan's pension (Part II)` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `a pension under Part IV (members of the Forces and peacekeepers)` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `an allowance or benefit under s 111 (other than bereavement payment)` THEN TRUE
            OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 9A(1): "A veteran's injury, disease or death is taken not to be war-caused if: (a) the injury is sustained, the disease is
-- contracted, or the death occurs, on or after the MRCA commencement date; and (b) the injury, disease or death either: (i) relates
-- to service rendered by the person on or after that date; or (ii) relates to service rendered by the person before, and on or
-- after, that date." Note: "compensation is provided under the MRCA (instead of this Act)". The MRCA commencement date is "the date
-- on which section 3 of the MRCA commences" (a borrowed term: asked as facts).
@export Is my injury, disease or death outside the Veterans' Entitlements Act because it falls under the MRCA (s 9A)?
GIVEN `it happened on or after the MRCA commencement date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the injury was sustained, the disease contracted, or the death occurred on or after the day the Military Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 2004 commenced
      `it relates to service on or after that date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it relates to service you rendered on or after that date (including service spanning it)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my injury the MRCA's, not the VEA's` IF
    `it happened on or after the MRCA commencement date` AND `it relates to service on or after that date`

§§ `s 5QA -- my pension age as a veteran`

-- s 5QA(2): "A man reaches pension age when he turns 60 years." (3): "A woman born before 1 July 1940 reaches pension age when she
-- turns 55." (4): the Table, from 55 years and 6 months (born 1 July 1940 to 31 December 1941) rising by 6 months every 18 months to
-- 59 years and 6 months (born 1 July 1952 to 31 December 1953). (5): "A woman born on or after 1 January 1954 reaches pension age when
-- she turns 60." (Persons other than veterans: s 5QB, not encoded.)
DECLARE `Man or woman` IS ONE OF
    `a man`
    `a woman`

@export What is my pension age as a veteran, in months (s 5QA)?
GIVEN `I am` IS A `Man or woman` @desc Whether you are a man or a woman
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your date of birth
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is my veteran pension age in months` MEANS
    CONSIDER `I am`
    WHEN `a man` THEN 720
    WHEN `a woman` THEN
        BRANCH IF `my date of birth` LESS THAN Date 1 7 1940 THEN 660
               IF `my date of birth` AT MOST Date 31 12 1941 THEN 666
               IF `my date of birth` AT MOST Date 30 6 1943 THEN 672
               IF `my date of birth` AT MOST Date 31 12 1944 THEN 678
               IF `my date of birth` AT MOST Date 30 6 1946 THEN 684
               IF `my date of birth` AT MOST Date 31 12 1947 THEN 690
               IF `my date of birth` AT MOST Date 30 6 1949 THEN 696
               IF `my date of birth` AT MOST Date 31 12 1950 THEN 702
               IF `my date of birth` AT MOST Date 30 6 1952 THEN 708
               IF `my date of birth` AT MOST Date 31 12 1953 THEN 714
               OTHERWISE 720

@export Have I reached pension age as a veteran on a given day (s 5QA)?
GIVEN `I am` IS A `Man or woman` @desc Whether you are a man or a woman
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your date of birth
      `the day` IS A DATE @desc The day you are asking about
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I reached veteran pension age` IF
    `complete months of age` `my date of birth` `the day` AT LEAST `What is my veteran pension age in months` `I am` `my date of birth`

§§ `s 7A -- have I rendered qualifying service`

-- s 7A(1)(a): a member of the Defence Force has rendered qualifying service who has "(i) rendered service, during a period of
-- hostilities [the World Wars] ..., at sea, in the field or in the air in naval, military or aerial operations against the enemy
-- ... at a time when the person incurred danger from hostile forces of the enemy ...; or (ii) rendered service after 29 October
-- 1945 in respect of which the person has been awarded, or has become eligible to be awarded, the Naval General Service Medal or
-- the General Service Medal ... with the Minesweeping 1945-51 Clasp [or a Bomb-Mine or Bomb and Mine Clearance Clasp]; or (iii)
-- rendered service outside Australia in an area described in column 1 of Schedule 2 during the period specified in column 2 ...
-- as a member of a unit ... that was allotted for duty, or as a person who was allotted for duty, in that area; or (iv) rendered
-- warlike service; or (v), (vi)" continuous full-time service on submarine special operations from 1 January 1978 to 12 May 1997
-- with (or eligible but for an earlier award of) the Australian Service Medal with Clasp "SPECIAL OPS". Paragraphs (b)-(h)
-- (Commonwealth and allied forces, special missions, detained civilians, mariners) are asked as one fact. "Warlike service" and
-- the Schedule 2 areas are asked as facts.
@export Have I rendered "qualifying service" for a service pension (s 7A)?
GIVEN `I served against the enemy in the World Wars and incurred danger` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, as a member of the Defence Force in World War 1 or 2, you served in operations against the enemy and incurred danger from hostile forces
      `I have a minesweeping or bomb and mine clearance clasp` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were awarded (or are eligible for) the Naval General Service Medal or General Service Medal with a Minesweeping 1945-51 or Bomb and Mine Clearance clasp
      `I was allotted for duty in a Schedule 2 area` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you served outside Australia, allotted for duty (yourself or your unit), in an area and period listed in Schedule 2 (for example Korea, Malaya, Vietnam)
      `I rendered warlike service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you rendered warlike service (service the Minister has declared warlike, for example in East Timor, Iraq or Afghanistan)
      `I served on submarine special operations 1978 to 1997` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you rendered continuous full-time service on submarine special operations between 1 January 1978 and 12 May 1997 with (or eligible for) the Australian Service Medal with Clasp SPECIAL OPS
      `another s 7A(1) limb applies to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether another limb applies: service in a Commonwealth or allied force, a special mission, a civilian detained by the enemy, or an Australian or allied mariner in danger
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I rendered qualifying service` IF
       `I served against the enemy in the World Wars and incurred danger`
    OR `I have a minesweeping or bomb and mine clearance clasp`
    OR `I was allotted for duty in a Schedule 2 area`
    OR `I rendered warlike service`
    OR `I served on submarine special operations 1978 to 1997`
    OR `another s 7A(1) limb applies to me`

§§ `ss 36, 37, 36H -- am I eligible for a service pension`

-- s 36(1): "a person is eligible for an age service pension if the person: (a) is a veteran; and (b) has rendered qualifying service;
-- and (c) has reached pension age." s 37(1): eligible for an invalidity service pension if "(a) is a veteran; and (b) has rendered
-- qualifying service; and (c) is permanently incapacitated for work in accordance with a determination under section 37AA" (the
-- Commission's instrument: a fact). ss 36(2), 37(3): a veteran "by reason only of being a Commonwealth veteran, an allied veteran or
-- an allied mariner must ... have been an Australian resident for a continuous period of at least 10 years", unless a refugee or
-- former refugee ((2A), (3A)). ss 36(3), 37(4): where "the longer or longest of those periods is less than 10 years but is not less
-- than 5 years; and (c) the aggregate of those periods is more than 10 years", the 10 years is "reduced by a period equal to the
-- period by which the aggregate is more than 10 years". s 37(5): the residence rule does not apply to invalidity service pension if
-- the incapacity began while an Australian resident, was not brought about to get a pension, and there is no enforceable claim for
-- adequate compensation for it.
DECLARE `What kind of veteran I am` IS ONE OF
    `an Australian veteran (Australian Defence Force or Australian mariner)`
    `a Commonwealth veteran, allied veteran or allied mariner only`

GIVEN `kind` IS A `What kind of veteran I am`
      `I am a refugee or former refugee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `my longest continuous residence in years` IS A NUMBER
      `my total residence in years` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `I meet the s 36(2) residence rule` IF
       `kind` EQUALS `an Australian veteran (Australian Defence Force or Australian mariner)`
    OR `I am a refugee or former refugee`
    OR `my longest continuous residence in years` AT LEAST 10
    OR (    `my longest continuous residence in years` AT LEAST 5
        AND `my total residence in years` GREATER THAN 10
        AND `my longest continuous residence in years` AT LEAST (10 MINUS (`my total residence in years` MINUS 10)))

@export Am I eligible for the age service pension (s 36)?
GIVEN `I have rendered qualifying service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have rendered qualifying service (see the qualifying service question, or a Commission determination under s 35J)
      `I have reached veteran pension age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have reached your pension age as a veteran (see the pension age questions)
      `kind` IS A `What kind of veteran I am` @desc Whether you are an Australian veteran, or a veteran only because you served in a Commonwealth or allied force or as an allied mariner
      `I am a refugee or former refugee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a refugee or former refugee
      `my longest continuous residence in years` IS A NUMBER @desc Your longest single period of Australian residence, in years
      `my total residence in years` IS A NUMBER @desc The total of all your periods of Australian residence, in years
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I eligible for the age service pension` IF
        `I have rendered qualifying service`
    AND `I have reached veteran pension age`
    AND `I meet the s 36(2) residence rule` `kind` `I am a refugee or former refugee` `my longest continuous residence in years` `my total residence in years`

@export Am I eligible for the invalidity service pension (s 37)?
GIVEN `I have rendered qualifying service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have rendered qualifying service
      `I am permanently incapacitated for work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are permanently incapacitated for work in the circumstances the Commission's s 37AA determination specifies
      `kind` IS A `What kind of veteran I am` @desc Whether you are an Australian veteran, or a veteran only through a Commonwealth or allied force or as an allied mariner
      `I am a refugee or former refugee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a refugee or former refugee
      `my longest continuous residence in years` IS A NUMBER @desc Your longest single period of Australian residence, in years
      `my total residence in years` IS A NUMBER @desc The total of all your periods of Australian residence, in years
      `my incapacity began here, unprovoked and uncompensated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you became permanently incapacitated while an Australian resident, not to obtain a pension, and you have no enforceable claim for adequate compensation for it
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I eligible for the invalidity service pension` IF
        `I have rendered qualifying service`
    AND `I am permanently incapacitated for work`
    AND (    `my incapacity began here, unprovoked and uncompensated`
          OR `I meet the s 36(2) residence rule` `kind` `I am a refugee or former refugee` `my longest continuous residence in years` `my total residence in years`)

-- s 36H(1): "a claim is not a proper claim unless the veteran ... is: (a) an Australian resident; and (b) in Australia; on the day on
-- which the claim is lodged." (2): unless the veteran is outside Australia receiving an invalidity or partner service pension,
-- income support supplement, veteran payment or a social security pension, and would be eligible for age service pension if it
-- were cancelled. s 36B(1), (1A): the pension "is not payable to a veteran before the veteran's provisional commencement day", which
-- "is the day on which the veteran claims"; (2): if an initial claim was not a proper claim but the veteran was eligible that day
-- and makes a proper claim "within 3 months after being notified that the initial claim was not a proper claim" (or at any time if
-- not notified), it is the day of the initial claim. "Within 3 months after" day N: on or before the same day 3 months later.
@export From what day can my age service pension be paid (s 36B)?
GIVEN `the day of my proper claim` IS A DATE @desc The day you lodged a proper claim (resident and in Australia, in the approved form)
      `I made an earlier claim that was not proper` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you first lodged a claim that was not a proper claim (for example on the wrong form)
      `the day of the earlier claim` IS A DATE @desc The day of that earlier claim (ignored otherwise)
      `I was eligible on the day of the earlier claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were already eligible for age service pension on the day of the earlier claim
      `I was told the earlier claim was not proper` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were notified that the earlier claim was not a proper claim
      `the day I was told` IS A DATE @desc The day you were notified (ignored if you were not)
GIVETH A DATE
`From what day can my age service pension be paid` MEANS
    IF     `I made an earlier claim that was not proper`
       AND `I was eligible on the day of the earlier claim`
       AND (    (NOT `I was told the earlier claim was not proper`)
             OR `the day of my proper claim` AT MOST (`the day months after` `the day I was told` 3))
    THEN `the day of the earlier claim`
    ELSE `the day of my proper claim`

§§ `ss 22, 23, 24 -- what rate of disability pension am I paid`

-- (Situation: I already receive, or had claimed before 1 July 2026, a disability pension for war-caused incapacity.)
-- s 22(2): the general rate pension is "the same percentage of the general rate as the percentage determined by the Commission in
-- accordance with section 21A to be the degree of incapacity"; (3): the general rate "is $338.94 per fortnight". (4): the extreme
-- disablement adjustment ("$510.40 per fortnight") if "(a)" the degree of incapacity is 100% (or pulmonary tuberculosis at the
-- maximum rate); "(b) the veteran has attained the age of 65; (c) the veteran has an impairment rating of at least 70 points and a
-- lifestyle rating of at least 6 points ...; and (d)" no s 23, 24 or 25 rate.
-- s 24(1): the special rate ("$1,595.66 per fortnight", (4)) if the claim was made before 65, "(a)" the degree of incapacity "is ...
-- at least 70%" (or tuberculosis), "(b) the veteran is totally and permanently incapacitated, that is to say, the veteran's
-- incapacity ... is of such a nature as, of itself alone, to render the veteran incapable of undertaking remunerative work for
-- periods aggregating more than 8 hours per week; and (c) the veteran is, by reason of [that] incapacity ... alone, prevented from
-- continuing to undertake remunerative work that the veteran was undertaking and is, by reason thereof, suffering a loss of salary
-- or wages". (2A): for a claim made at 65 or over, also "(f) the veteran was undertaking his or her last paid work after the veteran
-- had turned 65; and (g) ... had been undertaking remunerative work for a continuous period of at least 10 years that began before
-- the veteran turned 65". (3): also "a veteran who has been blinded in both eyes as a result of war-caused injury or war-caused
-- disease".
-- s 23(1): the intermediate rate ("$619.80 per fortnight", (4)) on the same terms, but where the incapacity makes the veteran
-- "incapable of undertaking remunerative work otherwise than on a part-time basis or intermittently", which (2) is not so if the
-- veteran can work "50 per centum or more of the time ... ordinarily worked" full-time (or 20 or more hours a week); (3A) for a
-- claim at 65 or over, the same (f) and (g).
-- Every rate is indexed (s 198): the rates in force are inputs. Section 25 (temporary special rate), ss 23(5), 24(5)-(6), 25A, 26,
-- 27 and 115D are not encoded.
DECLARE `How much I can work` IS ONE OF
    `no more than 8 hours a week, because of my war-caused incapacity alone`
    `only part-time or intermittently (under half of full-time hours, or under 20 hours a week), because of it alone`
    `more than that`

DECLARE `My rate of disability pension` IS ONE OF
    `the special rate (s 24), per fortnight` HAS `the amount` IS A NUMBER
    `the intermediate rate (s 23), per fortnight` HAS `the amount` IS A NUMBER
    `the extreme disablement adjustment rate (s 22(4)), per fortnight` HAS `the amount` IS A NUMBER
    `the general rate pension (s 22(2)): my degree of incapacity as a percentage of the general rate, per fortnight` HAS `the amount` IS A NUMBER

@export What rate of disability pension am I paid for my war-caused incapacity, and how much a fortnight (ss 22, 23, 24)?
GIVEN `my degree of incapacity` IS A NUMBER @desc Your degree of incapacity from war-caused injury or disease as a percentage, as the Repatriation Commission has assessed it under the Approved Guide (for example 70)
      `I am blinded in both eyes by it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have been blinded in both eyes as a result of war-caused injury or disease
      `how much I can work` IS A `How much I can work` @desc How much remunerative work your war-caused incapacity alone leaves you able to do
      `it stopped my work and I lost earnings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your war-caused incapacity alone stopped you continuing the paid work you were doing, so that you lost earnings (or, under 65 and not working, you were genuinely seeking work and it is the substantial cause of not getting it)
      `I claimed before turning 65` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you made the claim (or application for increase) before you turned 65
      `my last job was after 65 after 10 years' work begun before 65` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you claimed at 65 or over: whether your last paid work was after you turned 65, and when it stopped you had worked continuously for at least 10 years starting before 65
      `my age` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age now, in years
      `my impairment points` IS A NUMBER @desc Your impairment rating in points under the Approved Guide
      `my lifestyle points` IS A NUMBER @desc Your lifestyle rating in points under the Approved Guide
      `the general rate in force` IS A NUMBER @desc The general rate of disability pension per fortnight as indexed (s 22(3) prints $338.94)
      `the EDA rate in force` IS A NUMBER @desc The extreme disablement adjustment rate per fortnight as indexed (s 22(4) prints $510.40)
      `the intermediate rate in force` IS A NUMBER @desc The intermediate rate per fortnight as indexed (s 23(4) prints $619.80)
      `the special rate in force` IS A NUMBER @desc The special (TPI) rate per fortnight as indexed (s 24(4) prints $1,595.66)
GIVETH A `My rate of disability pension`
`What rate of disability pension am I paid` MEANS
    IF `I am blinded in both eyes by it` OR (`the work tests are met` AND `how much I can work` EQUALS `no more than 8 hours a week, because of my war-caused incapacity alone`)
    THEN `the special rate (s 24), per fortnight` `the special rate in force`
    ELSE IF `the work tests are met` AND `how much I can work` EQUALS `only part-time or intermittently (under half of full-time hours, or under 20 hours a week), because of it alone`
         THEN `the intermediate rate (s 23), per fortnight` `the intermediate rate in force`
         ELSE IF `my degree of incapacity` AT LEAST 100 AND `my age` AT LEAST 65 AND `my impairment points` AT LEAST 70 AND `my lifestyle points` AT LEAST 6
              THEN `the extreme disablement adjustment rate (s 22(4)), per fortnight` `the EDA rate in force`
              ELSE `the general rate pension (s 22(2)): my degree of incapacity as a percentage of the general rate, per fortnight` (((min `my degree of incapacity` 100) DIVIDED BY 100) TIMES `the general rate in force`)
    WHERE
        `the work tests are met` MEANS
                `my degree of incapacity` AT LEAST 70
            AND `it stopped my work and I lost earnings`
            AND (`I claimed before turning 65` OR `my last job was after 65 after 10 years' work begun before 65`)

§§ `ss 13A, 30(1) -- a war widow's or widower's pension when the veteran dies`

-- (Situation: the veteran has died; I am the widow or widower.)
-- s 13A(1): if the veteran "was, immediately before the veteran's death, a veteran to whom subsection 22(4) or section 23, 24 or 25
-- applied" (or on a s 22 pension increased by s 27 items 1-8), the pension payable to the dependant "is payable: (d) without the
-- dependant having to make a claim ... and (e) without the Commission having to make a determination". (2): "The pension is payable
-- from and including the day after the veteran died." s 13(2): the Commonwealth is liable for a dependant's pension where the death
-- was not war-caused but the veteran was on one of those rates; s 13(1): where the death was war-caused. s 30(1): the widow's or
-- widower's rate is "(a) 1/26 of the amount specified in column 3 of item 1 of the table in point SCH6-B1 of Schedule 6; (b) $35;
-- (c) $25.60" per fortnight, all indexed (inputs). Since 1 July 2026 a new claim under Part II cannot be made (s 12AA), so the
-- automatic payment of s 13A matters most.
DECLARE `My war widow's or widower's pension` IS ONE OF
    `paid automatically, without a claim, from the day after the veteran died (s 13A)` HAS `the first day` IS A DATE
    `not automatic under s 13A; from 1 July 2026 a claim for it is made under the MRCA, not this Act (s 12AA)`
    `not automatic under s 13A; a claim under s 14 was possible before 1 July 2026`

@export My partner, a veteran, has died. Do I get a war widow's or widower's pension without claiming, and from when (s 13A)?
GIVEN `the veteran was on the EDA, intermediate, special or temporary special rate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, just before the death, the veteran was paid the extreme disablement adjustment or the intermediate, special (TPI) or temporary special rate (or a general rate increased for a s 27 items 1-8 disability)
      `the day the veteran died` IS A DATE @desc The day the veteran died
GIVETH A `My war widow's or widower's pension`
`Do I get a war widow's pension without claiming` MEANS
    IF `the veteran was on the EDA, intermediate, special or temporary special rate`
    THEN `paid automatically, without a claim, from the day after the veteran died (s 13A)` (`the day the veteran died` PLUS 1)
    ELSE IF `the day the veteran died` AT LEAST Date 1 7 2026
         THEN `not automatic under s 13A; from 1 July 2026 a claim for it is made under the MRCA, not this Act (s 12AA)`
         ELSE `not automatic under s 13A; a claim under s 14 was possible before 1 July 2026`

@export What is my war widow's or widower's pension a fortnight (s 30(1))?
GIVEN `the annual pension MBR in force` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount in column 3 of item 1 of the table in point SCH6-B1 of Schedule 6 (the single service pension maximum basic rate a year) as indexed, in dollars
      `the s 30(1)(b) amount in force` IS A NUMBER @desc The s 30(1)(b) amount as indexed (printed as $35)
      `the s 30(1)(c) amount in force` IS A NUMBER @desc The s 30(1)(c) amount as indexed (printed as $25.60)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is my war widow's pension a fortnight` MEANS
    (`the annual pension MBR in force` DIVIDED BY 26) PLUS `the s 30(1)(b) amount in force` PLUS `the s 30(1)(c) amount in force`

§§ `s 54 -- telling the Department`

-- (Situation: I receive a service pension, income support supplement or veteran payment, or have claimed one.)
-- s 54(1): the Secretary may give a notice requiring the person to inform the Department if a specified event or change occurs; (5):
-- the period "must end not later than 14 days after: (a) the day on which the event or change of circumstances occurs; or (b) the day
-- on which the person becomes aware that [it] is likely to occur"; (5A): in special circumstances, 15 to 28 days as the Secretary
-- directs. (6): an offence, "Imprisonment for 6 months or 10 penalty units, or both", strict liability, not to the extent the
-- person cannot comply (8).
@export I have a notice to report changes on my service pension. What is the latest day the notice can give me to report a change (s 54)?
GIVEN `the day of the change` IS A DATE @desc The day the event or change happened (or you became aware it is likely to happen)
      `the Secretary directed a special period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Secretary directed a longer period because of special circumstances
      `the days the Secretary directed` IS A NUMBER @desc If so: the number of days directed (between 15 and 28)
GIVETH A DATE
`What is the latest day to report a change` MEANS
    IF `the Secretary directed a special period`
    THEN `the day of the change` PLUS (max 15 (min 28 `the days the Secretary directed`))
    ELSE `the day of the change` PLUS 14

§§ `ss 57, 57A, 135(5), 175 -- asking for review`

-- s 57: a person dissatisfied with a decision about a service pension, income support supplement or veteran payment (cancelling,
-- suspending, reducing, refusing an increase, financial hardship ...) "may request the Commission to review the decision". s 57A(1):
-- the request must "(a) be made within 3 months after the person seeking review was notified of the decision; and (b) set out the
-- grounds ...; and (c) be in writing; and (d) be lodged at an office of the Department in Australia". s 175(2): then the ART.
-- s 135(5): an application to the Veterans' Review Board under Part 4 of Chapter 8 of the MRCA about a disability pension's rate
-- (assessing, refusing for insufficient incapacity, refusing to increase, reducing, cancelling or suspending) "may be made within 3
-- months after service on the person ... of a copy of that decision ..., but not otherwise". Other Part II review time limits are
-- the MRCA's (not encoded). "Within 3 months after" day N: by the same day 3 months later.
DECLARE `The decision I want reviewed` IS ONE OF
    `a decision about my service pension, income support supplement or veteran payment`
    `a decision about the rate of my disability pension, or cancelling or suspending it`

DECLARE `How I can seek review` IS ONE OF
    `ask the Repatriation Commission in writing, with grounds, lodged at a Department office in Australia, within 3 months after I was notified (s 57A); then the ART (s 175(2)). Last day:` HAS `the last day` IS A DATE
    `apply to the Veterans' Review Board under Chapter 8 of the MRCA within 3 months after I was served with the decision, but not later (s 135(5)). Last day:` HAS `the last day` IS A DATE

@export How, and by when, can I ask for review of a decision about my veterans' pension?
GIVEN `the decision` IS A `The decision I want reviewed` @desc Which decision you want reviewed
      `the day I was notified` IS A DATE @desc The day you were notified of the decision (or served with a copy of it)
GIVETH A `How I can seek review`
`How can I seek review of my veterans' pension decision` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the decision`
    WHEN `a decision about my service pension, income support supplement or veteran payment` THEN
        `ask the Repatriation Commission in writing, with grounds, lodged at a Department office in Australia, within 3 months after I was notified (s 57A); then the ART (s 175(2)). Last day:` (`the day months after` `the day I was notified` 3)
    WHEN `a decision about the rate of my disability pension, or cancelling or suspending it` THEN
        `apply to the Veterans' Review Board under Chapter 8 of the MRCA within 3 months after I was served with the decision, but not later (s 135(5)). Last day:` (`the day months after` `the day I was notified` 3)
